{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver gave the rider in-app notice before he deviated, which is what POL-RD-21 requires. MSG-05009-003 — 'Hi, BKE got accident near Dairy Farm, I take Woodlands Road ok?' — was sent at 15:49:39 through the IN_APP channel and read at 15:49:50, and the trip record's own derived messages_during_trip block lists that message and the rider's reply as in-trip messages under POL-RD-21. The vehicle's first Woodlands Road fix is not until 15:51:49, so the notice preceded the deviation rather than following it. The chat-log artifact is COMPLETE at weight 1.0 and its 4 entries match trip_record.chat_message_count.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05009", "EV-TRIP-05009", "EV-GPS-05009"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.messages_during_trip",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider acknowledged the reroute in the same channel and in advance of it. MSG-05009-004, 'ok can', was sent at 15:49:59 — twenty seconds after the driver's message — while the platform's own deviation event is timestamped 15:51:59 and the first Woodlands Road fix 15:51:49. POL-RD-21 provides that where the chat log confirms the rider's acknowledgment the deviation is agreed; on this record the Woodlands Road leg is an agreed deviation, and the rider cannot now treat as unconsented the extra distance she accepted while sitting in the car.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05009", "EV-TRIP-05009", "EV-GPS-05009"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.events.route_deviation_detected",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The only traffic data in this record is EV-ADVIS-05009-01 and it is MISSING; I disclose that it carries the issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT and a weight_multiplier of 0.0, and that under POL-GEN-02 a MISSING artifact carries no fact. Its own derived block records why: the platform's request to the LTA historical traffic feed timed out and was not retried, so the record is 'silent on traffic on the recommended route; this is not a finding of no traffic'. Traffic justification under POL-RD-23 therefore cannot be established either way on this record — the driver's assertion of a jam alone would not justify the reroute, but neither does an absent advisory establish that the BKE was clear.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05009-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-23", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "traffic_advisory.derived.v7.available",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's case rests on her own search for accident news after the trip, which is not the traffic data POL-RD-23 requires (a TRAFFIC_ADVISORY intersecting the recommended route and overlapping the trip window) and says nothing about this trip's road conditions at 15:50 on 23 August 2026. Under POL-GEN-26 no outcome is inferred from the absence of evidence, so her failure to find a news report no more shows the BKE was clear than the missing LTA record shows it was congested. The rider has produced no traffic data; she has produced the absence of a search result.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05009-01", "EV-TRIP-05009"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-23", "POL-GEN-26"],
      "relies_on": "traffic_advisory.derived.v7.justifies_reroute",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-24 requires exactly one row to apply, and the only refund row capable of reaching this trip — row (d), 'not traffic-justified, deviation over 1 km' — depends on a positive finding that the reroute was not justified. This record cannot make that finding: the traffic artifact is MISSING at weight 0.0 and is expressly not a finding of no traffic, POL-GEN-02 says it carries no fact, and POL-GEN-26 forbids inferring an outcome from the absence of evidence. With row (a) unavailable for want of the traffic data and row (d)'s predicate unestablished, the case fits no row, and POL-RD-24's own closing sentence routes a case that fits no row to escalation under POL-GEN-26.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05009-01", "EV-TRIP-05009"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24", "POL-GEN-26", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.deviation.within_tolerance",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Escalation is the driver-protective outcome here, and it is the outcome POL-GEN-03 defines: ESCALATE is terminal, no monetary outcome issues, and the amount is held. The ledger shows payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so there is nothing to restore and the metered fare of 14.05 SGD stays where it is while a human reviewer retrieves the LTA feed that the platform failed to obtain. NO_ACTION would equally leave the charge standing, because the rider filed and the charge has not been refunded.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05009", "EV-TRIP-05009"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "If the judge nevertheless finds that a refund row applies, POL-RD-24 fixes the refund at the excess distance fare — deviation_km times fare_breakdown.per_km_rate_sgd, without surge — which on this record is 1.50 km x 0.72 SGD = 1.08 SGD, not the 3.50 SGD the rider asks for. The 3.15 SGD time fare for 17.5 minutes is not part of that measure, and FULL_REFUND under POL-GEN-03 would require the filer to be entirely right, which on an in-app agreed deviation she is not. The rider's exposure is at most a 1.08 SGD partial refund on a 14.05 SGD fare.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05009", "EV-TRIP-05009"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24", "POL-RD-22", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.excess_distance_fare_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The deviation itself is minor and was not an abandonment of the route. On POL-RD-22's recorded-distance method it is 1.50 km on an 8.5 km recommended route (10.0 km actual less 8.5 km optimal), and the driver-device trace shows one continuous detour along Woodlands Road, Bukit Panjang Road and Petir Road, rejoining the recommended route at Petir Road at 16:03:01 before drop-off at Hillion Mall. Even under the v2.1 6.2 limb held in POL-RD-25 — which is not applied in this case, ai_ruling_max_deviation_applied being false — a 2.0 km ceiling would not be crossed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05009", "EV-GPS-05009"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-22", "POL-RD-25"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.deviation.deviation_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "Both of you: this case goes to a human reviewer. No money moves now — the SGD 3.50 in dispute is held rather than refunded to the rider or kept for the driver.\n\nWhat is not in dispute. Trip TRP-05009 was booked from Causeway Point to Hillion Mall with a recommended route of 8.5 km via the BKE. The platform's trip record (EV-TRIP-05009, weight 1.0) records 10.0 km actually driven, so on POL-RD-22's recorded-distance method the deviation is 1.50 km — over the 1.0 km tolerance — and the driver-device trace (EV-GPS-05009, weight 1.0) confirms the route taken: Woodlands Road from about 15:51:49, rejoining at Bukit Panjang Road and Petir Road at 16:03:01 before drop-off. The fare charged was SGD 14.05, the per-km rate SGD 0.72, and the excess-distance figure POL-RD-24 derives is 1.50 x 0.72 = SGD 1.08.\n\nNotice and acknowledgment — the driver's point, accepted. Under POL-RD-21 the driver must inform the rider before or at the point of deviation, and where the chat log confirms the rider's acknowledgment the deviation is agreed. MSG-05009-003 ('Hi, BKE got accident near Dairy Farm, I take Woodlands Road ok?') was sent in-app at 15:49:39, before the first Woodlands Road fix at 15:51:49, with a brief reason, and MSG-05009-004 ('ok can') came at 15:49:59. On POL-RD-21's own test the chat log (EV-CHAT-05009, weight 1.0) confirms both notice and acknowledgment. The rider's argument that the acknowledgment should not count because the accident was unverified does not succeed: POL-RD-21 makes the chat log the test, and it is met.\n\nWhat cannot be decided, and why the case escalates. Every no-refund row of POL-RD-24 — (a), (b) and (c) — requires the reroute to be traffic-justified, and row (d), the refund row, requires a positive finding that it was not. POL-RD-23 allows traffic justification only on a TRAFFIC_ADVISORY intersecting the recommended route and overlapping the trip window. The only such artifact, EV-ADVIS-05009-01, is MISSING: weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — the platform's LTA feed request timed out and was not retried, and the record states in terms that its silence 'is not a finding of no traffic'. A MISSING artifact carries no fact (POL-GEN-02(3)). The traffic limb is therefore undecided: it cannot carry row (a), (b) or (c) for the driver, and because the rider's row (d) needs a finding the record cannot make, it cannot carry a refund either. The driver's bare assertion of a jam would not by itself justify the reroute, but neither does a failed retrieval prove the BKE was clear. POL-RD-24 provides that a case fitting no row is escalated under POL-GEN-26, and POL-GEN-26 names 'whether traffic justified the reroute' as exactly the kind of fact whose evidence is missing. So ESCALATE, which is terminal: no monetary outcome issues and the amount is held. The rider's claim that the reroute is 'not traffic-justified' is rejected for that reason; the rider's alternative claim that POL-GEN-26 requires escalation is accepted, as are the driver's claims that the traffic data is missing and that escalation is the correct outcome. The driver's fallback that a refund, if a row applied, would be SGD 1.08 and not the SGD 3.50 asked for is arithmetically correct and is recorded for the reviewer, but no refund row applies.\n\nWho decides and with what confidence. The contested value is SGD 3.50, below POL-GEN-22's SGD 10.00 band, so no value uplift applies, and both profiles show fraud_flags of 0; the deviation of 1.50 km is below POL-RD-25's held 2.0 km ceiling (ai_ruling_max_deviation_applied is false). POL-RD-25's 0.80 confidence bar is met at 0.85, but the escalation follows from POL-GEN-26 in any event. Open question for the reviewer: obtain the LTA traffic record for the recommended BKE route for 23 August 2026 between 15:46 and 16:04, then apply POL-RD-24's matrix. No referral is issued, because none of the clauses that produce one (POL-NS-24, POL-NS-25, POL-NS-22) arises here."
  },
